{
    "description": "Boundary coverage for callback (function) targets: a flush with no further events invokes the callback once, and because a function target has no value-equality guard a repeated value still re-invokes it (here flush plus one identical change yields two invocations).",
    "cases": [
        {
            "input": {
                "action": "bind",
                "source_type": "property",
                "target_type": "function",
                "initial": "foo",
                "flush": true,
                "events": ["bar"]
            },
            "expected_output": "value=bar\nupdates=2\n"
        },
        {
            "input": {
                "action": "bind",
                "source_type": "property",
                "target_type": "function",
                "initial": "foo",
                "flush": true,
                "events": ["foo"]
            },
            "expected_output": "value=foo\nupdates=2\n"
        }
    ]
}
